# Tokens only

`Sources/Design/` is the single source of truth. Raw literals in a view are a
gate failure (`system_fonts`, `raw_colors`, `raw_radius`, `offgrid_spacing`).

| Need | Use | Never |
|---|---|---|
| Color | `BeruColor.canvas` `.surface` `.border` `.textPrimary` `.textSecondary` `.accent` `.onAccent` `.positive` `.destructive` | `Color(red:)`, `.secondary`, `.primary.opacity(0.85)` |
| Type | `BeruType.pageTitle` `.section` `.rowTitle` `.body` `.footnote` `.caption` `.mono` | `.font(.system(size: 11))`, `.headline`, `.caption` |
| Space | `BeruSpace.hair/xxs/xs/sm/md/lg/xl/xxl` = 2/4/8/12/16/24/32/48 | `spacing: 5`, `padding(14)` |
| Radius | `BeruRadius.sm/md/lg/xl` = 6/10/16/20, always `.continuous` | `cornerRadius(10)`, `.circular` |
| Geometry | `BeruMetrics` | duplicate window/panel constants |

```swift
// BAD
VStack(spacing: 6) { Text(t).font(.system(size: 11)).foregroundStyle(.secondary) }
    .padding(14)
    .background(Color(red: 0.125, green: 0.13, blue: 0.16))

// GOOD
VStack(spacing: BeruSpace.xxs) { Text(t).font(BeruType.caption).foregroundStyle(BeruColor.textSecondary) }
    .padding(BeruSpace.md)
    .background(BeruColor.surface)
```

# One button system

Use `BeruButton` variants (`.primary`, `.pill`, `.inline`, `.icon`). Do not add
`.borderedProminent` or `.bordered` next to Beru capsules, and do not hand-roll
a new capsule.

# Off the grid

If a value genuinely needs to be off-grid, add a named token in `Sources/Design`
with a comment explaining why. Do not inline the number.

# Panel height contract (frozen)

Window height = min(chrome + resultIdeal, **75%** of the screen’s visible
height). Chrome = close strip + chips + composer (+ 10pt insets/spacings).
Only the result band grows with text; at the cap it scrolls inside
`AppState.panelResultScrollHeight` while chrome stays pinned.

Grow immediately; shrink after a short debounce. `moduleInset` /
`moduleSpacing` stay at 10. `maxViewportFraction` stays at `0.75`.

Do not:
- drive height from `NSHostingView.intrinsicContentSize` / `sizingOptions`
- put close / chips / composer inside the result `ScrollView`
- measure the root inside a flexible infinite max-height frame
- re-impose a comfort `minHeight` after the first measure
- animate window resize on tab change
- hide toolbar context with `if` (use opacity)
- change `maxViewportFraction` without updating `PanelViewportCapTests` and QA

At the viewport cap, scroll the result — never clip the composer.

# Enforced by scripts/qa.sh

The contract above used to be prose only, so nothing caught a regression. These
guards now fail the gate:

- `panel_intrinsic_sizing` — no `sizingOptions = [.…]` in `Sources/Panel`.
  `PanelController` sets `sizingOptions = []` deliberately; height comes from
  child preferences.
- `panel_chrome_min_height` — no `minHeight:` literals in `Sources/Panel`. A
  comfort minimum re-imposed after the first measure locks the window open.
- `glass_on_glass` — `glassEffect` only in `Sources/Design` and
  `GlassStyles.swift`. Apple forbids stacking glass on glass; inner modules use
  `.glassModule(…)`, which is an overlay, not a second slab.
- `panel_inline_key_handling` — no `press.modifiers.contains(…)` in
  `Sources/Panel`. `PanelKeyBinding` owns the decision table so it can be tested
  without a host view; a bare Return must never resolve to a destructive replace.
- `unmanaged_status_writes` — `statusMessage` is assigned only inside
  `VaultStore`. Use `flashStatus(_:)`, which expires the banner; direct writes
  left it on screen forever.
- `offgrid_frames` — raw `.frame(width:)` / `.frame(height:)` numbers off the
  4pt grid. The `offgrid_spacing` guard only reads `spacing:` and `padding(`, so
  frames were invisible to it. The current count is not yet zero and may only
  fall; put a genuine exception in `Sources/Design` as a named token.
